OL,3,GNEWSA'I was too worried to use the bus
OL,4,Abefore training'
OL,5,
OL,6,F"My parents are really proud of how far
OL,7,FI've come," says Zak, who has a
OL,8,Flearning disability and can can now
OL,9,Ftravel to college independently thanks
OL,10,Fto a training programme.
OL,12,FHe is one of a growing number of
OL,13,Fteenagers receiving one-to-one support
OL,14,Fto help them use public transport to
OL,15,Fget to their place of study.
OL,17,F"I was really worried about crowding
OL,18,Fand [thinking] what if the bus is late
OL,19,For it's cancelled," says 16-year-old
OL,20,FEloise, who has autism.
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
